From d9d2b89b50d859d2310d04e32e988390f83b16b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 12:36:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10903/11362] Update the doc/YAML pattern: 12-task plans emit
 whole, 14-task plans truncate

Milestone 608 planned 12 and emitted 12. With 605 also 12-and-12, and 606 and
607 both planning 14 and emitting 4 and 7, the split on planned task count is
now perfect in both directions across four milestones with no counterexample.

That is the strongest support yet for the budget reading in the previous
correction, and it is worth recording precisely because I have already had to
retract one narrowing on this same question. Still four milestones. Still not
established.

Names the two things that would settle it, cheapest first: the record-wide
sweep of document count against YAML count across every milestone rather than
only the measured ones, and a 13-task plan, which the record does not contain
and which would locate the boundary instead of bracketing it between 12 and 14.

Records what the evidence now rules out, since a reader of the first entry alone
would still believe all three: the divergence is not random, it does not require
a preceding planner timeout because 607 had none, and it is not a fixed YAML
size because it produced 4 and then 7.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
